{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793201228,"nonce":"M07H+AzegH1gP6eHJB+28AdNpa0=","message":"Completed checkpoints on main:\n- 73322d47: persistent lowered/optimized AIR cache for native and WASM AOT.\n- 9bd0de0a: separate linker stage timers and corrected AOT reachability documentation.\n- 501f2ade: share bounded preparation state within a build.\n- c485a4e7: observe integer proof dependencies, resolve constant/global payloads afresh in codegen, coalesce LRU timestamp writes.\n\nFinal checks: 9 cache unit tests, 3 release CLI process tests (including native/WASM text-only edits and WASM function edits), 226 AIR tests and 40 linker/fiber tests passed. Two concurrent CLI builds produced correct output with no cache errors. Final warm and edited Ashui applications passed the headless Chrome smoke and exited 0. Disabled/cold/warm WASM hashes are identical; edited output also matches the previously validated edited hash.\n\nFinal isolated WindowPage samples: disabled 20.175 s, cold 20.526 s, warm 20.906 s, function edit 25.326 s. Warm reuses all 3,552 optimized bodies with no AIR lowering/passes/writes. Edit reuses 3,551, with 2 misses/writes (lowered + optimized), 0.031 ms lowering and 0.375 ms passes. Final cache: 7,106 files, 5,271,419 serialized bytes. Peak whole-process RSS 1.50-2.21 GiB across these samples.\n\nNo consistent overall build-time speedup is claimed for this application: cache reads replace its small AIR bill, while LLVM is the largest cost and varies across samples. Warm LLVM backend 13.486 s; whole WASM link 1.030 s, including input parse 39.657 ms, resolve 50.909 ms, layout/reachability 275.180 ms, relocations 66.649 ms, emission 44.591 ms, and fibers 542.473 ms. The cache implementation, controls, bounds, invalidation and behavior requirements are complete. LLVM WASM compilation speed is being researched separately at the user's request.\n\nFull report and reproduction: docs/wasm/air-cache-build-times.md and scripts/bench_air_cache.py. The report explicitly separates AIR reuse from overall build latency and explains the reflection-root limitation of the current diagnostic reachability analysis.","files":null}]}